Search query: "How to search for a string in an array in JavaScript?"

To search for a string in an array in JavaScript, you can use the following code snippet:

```javascript
let array = ["apple", "banana", "cherry"];
let searchString = "banana";

let result = array.filter(item => item === searchString);

if (result.length > 0) {
    console.log(`Element ${result[0]} found`);
} else {
    console.log(`Element ${searchString} not found`);
}
```

This algorithm checks if the search string is present in the array and prints the result accordingly.

